---
import { path } from '../lib/path';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Strategy & Philosophy — Iron Hold Capital">
  <section class="page-header container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our Philosophy</p>
    <h1>Protect first. Grow always.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="prose container">
    <p>
      Iron Hold Capital was built on a simple premise: most capital is lost not to
      bad markets, but to bad discipline. We combine three asset classes that
      rarely move together &mdash; digital assets, gold, and actively traded
      global markets &mdash; into a single, risk-managed approach.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each pillar plays a distinct role. Gold anchors the portfolio against
      uncertainty. Digital assets capture asymmetric, longer-horizon opportunity.
      Global trading strategies stay active where markets are inefficient enough
      to reward it. None of the three is a bet on a single outcome &mdash;
      together, they are built to hold their ground across cycles.
    </p>

    <h2>How we think about risk</h2>
    <p>
      Position sizing comes before conviction. No single asset, trade, or theme
      is ever allowed to threaten the whole. Downside discipline governs every
      decision before upside potential is considered &mdash; concentration is a
      risk to be managed, not a strategy to be pursued.
    </p>

    <a href={path('/approach')} class="link-arrow">See how this plays out across our three pillars</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 64px 0 40px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 46px);
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 680px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 26px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 40px 0 16px;
  }
</style>
